# Requests to try with VS Code's REST Client extension.
# Start the server first (npm start, or npm run dev for readable logs), then click Send Request above any request.
# Watch the server's terminal: every request gets a log line, and the token below shows as [Redacted].

### Every route: 200
GET http://localhost:3100/routes

### One route by its id: 200
GET http://localhost:3100/routes/blue-loop

### A route that doesn't exist: 404
GET http://localhost:3100/routes/purple-line

### The health check: 200 { "status": "ok" } while MongoDB answers (503 { "status": "unavailable" } when it doesn't)
GET http://localhost:3100/health

### A request with a token: its Authorization header is logged as [Redacted]
GET http://localhost:3100/routes
Authorization: Bearer example-token-not-a-real-one
